/-!
# The Ext-side half of the last step of Stacks 0DXU

Fix an algebraization situation whose ring `A` is Noetherian local with `𝔞 = 𝔪` and which has a
normalized dualizing complex `ω`, let `I = (f)` be generated by a nonzerodivisor, and let `(ℱₙ)`
be a coherent `I`-adic system on `U = Spec(A) ∖ {𝔪}` whose terms are finite locally free over the
infinitesimal neighbourhoods they are annihilated by — hypotheses (1)–(4) of
[Stacks, Tag 0DXU] — satisfying in addition that tag's hypotheses

* (5) `depth((A/fA)_𝔭) + dim(A/𝔭) > 1` for every `𝔭 ∈ V(f)` other than `𝔪`, and
* (6) `depth(A_𝔭) + dim(A/𝔭) > 3` for every `𝔭 ∉ V(f)` with `V(𝔭) ∩ V(f) ≠ {𝔪}`.

Writing `Mₙ = H⁰(U, ℱₙ)`, this file proves that for some `n` the image of

  `Ext^{-2}_A(M₀, ω) ⟶ Ext^{-2}_A(Mₙ, ω)`

has finite length as an `A`-module — the last three paragraphs of the proof of that tag, after
local duality and Matlis duality have turned the tag's remaining condition into this one.

## Main results

* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.exists_isFiniteLength_range_of_forall_exists_smul_eq_zero` — one index
  serves every prime at once, by the ascending chain condition on the kernels.  This is what the
  source gets from its Lemma 52.5.2.
* `Dualizing.exists_pow_smul_moduleExtInto_eq_zero_of_depthDimOffDivisor` — hypothesis (6) makes
  `f` nilpotent on `H^{-k}(ω^•_{A_𝔮})` when `k + dim(A/𝔮) ≤ 3`: the source's "condition (6) tells
  us these primes are contained in `V(f)`".
* `Dualizing.exists_forall_ext_precomp_localized_eq_zero` — the three cases on `dim(A/𝔮)`.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.exists_isFiniteLength_range_extPrecompGlobalSections` — **the
  conclusion**.

## Implementation notes

The degree bookkeeping is `Dualizing.comp_eq_zero_of_comp_shift_eq_zero`.  The normalized dualizing
complex of `A_𝔮` is `(ω)_𝔮⟦-dim(A/𝔮)⟧` ([Stacks, Tag 0A7Z],
`Dualizing.isNormalizedDualizingComplex_localizedModule_shift`), so the degree `-2` into `(ω)_𝔮` is
the degree `-2 + dim(A/𝔮)` into the normalized complex, and the three cases of the source are
`dim(A/𝔮) ≥ 3`, where that degree is positive and both `Ext` modules vanish, and
`dim(A/𝔮) ∈ {1, 2}`, where it is `-k + 1` for `k ∈ {2, 1}` and the long exact sequence is needed.
The case `dim(A/𝔮) = 0` does not occur
(`Dualizing.one_le_ringKrullDim_quotient_of_ne_closedPoint`).

Universal catenarity, which
`Stacks.RingTheory.PrincipalDivisorDepth.depth_add_ringKrullDim_quotient_le` and
`ringKrullDim_quotient_eq_ringKrullDim_localization_add` need, is **not** carried as a hypothesis:
a Noetherian ring with a dualizing complex is universally catenary
([Stacks, Tag 0A80], `Dualizing.isUniversallyCatenary_of_isDualizingComplex`), so hypothesis (2)
discharges it.

[Stacks, Tag 0DWZ] part (4) describes the support of `H^{-k}(ω^•_{A_𝔮})` by primes `𝔓` of `A_𝔮`
with `depth((A_𝔮)_𝔓) + dim(A_𝔮/𝔓) ≤ k`.  Reading that back over `A` needs the correspondence
between the primes of `A_𝔮` and the primes of `A` below `𝔮`: `𝔓 = 𝔭A_𝔮` for
`𝔭 = 𝔓 ∩ A`, the localization `(A_𝔮)_𝔓` is `A_𝔭`
(`IsLocalization.localizationLocalizationAtPrimeIsoLocalization`, through
`Module.depth_self_eq_of_ringEquiv`), and `A_𝔮/𝔭A_𝔮` is `(A/𝔭)_𝔮`
(`Stacks.AdicCompletionDimension.ringKrullDim_quotient_localizationAtPrime`).  The support of
`H^{-k}` alone, rather than of the direct sum `H^0 ⊕ ⋯ ⊕ H^{-k}` that the tag describes, is
reached by `Dualizing.support_subset_support_pi`.

The local structure hypothesis (4) provides at a prime `𝔮 ∈ V(f) ∖ {𝔪}` — the localization
`(Mₙ)_𝔮` is a free `A_𝔮/f^{n+1}`-module, and the transition `(Mₙ)_𝔮 ⟶ (M₀)_𝔮` is surjective with
kernel `f(Mₙ)_𝔮` — is
`Stacks.Algebraization.exists_linearEquiv_quotSMulTop_localizedModule_globalSectionsSystem` and
`Stacks.Algebraization.surjective_and_ker_localizedModule_map_globalSectionsSystem`
(`…/CompletionCriteria/PrincipalLocalFreeStructure.lean`), which read the stalk of `ℱₙ` at the
point of `U` under `𝔮` back to `(Mₙ)_𝔮`.  The vanishing out of a free quotient that the two
long-exact-sequence cases consume is
`Dualizing.ext_precomp_eq_zero_of_isoQuotPow`.  Note that no basis of `(Mₙ)_𝔮` compatible with
the transition maps is needed — only the kernel of the transition — which is why the main theorem
asks for nothing of that kind.

The applications of `Dualizing.localizedExtLinearEquivOfDerivedHom` and its naturality are written
with `@` and explicit `inferInstance` arguments.  The `A`-module structure on the carrier of
`(globalSectionsSystem S F).obj (op n)` is reached through `ModuleCat.restrictScalars`, and
instance synthesis finds it when the expected type is already known but not when it has to be
discovered while unifying the implicit ring of a lemma about bare module types.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DXU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DXU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DWZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DWZ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A7Z](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A7Z)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A80](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A80)
-/

